      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "If $\\csc x = 2$, then what is $\\csc (x + 24π)$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The period of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=12$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\cdot 12\\cdot \\pi )=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+24\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=2,$ then $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+24\\pi )=2.$",
