      ":question/worked-solution": "The period of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=12$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\cdot 12\\cdot \\pi )=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+24\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=9,$ then $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+24\\pi )=9.$\n\nSubstituting $n=-5$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\cdot (-5)\\cdot \\pi )=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-10\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=9,$ then $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-10\\pi )=9.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+24\\pi )-4-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-10\\pi ) & =\\frac{3}{4}(9)-4-\\frac{2}{3}(9) \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{4}-4-6 \\\\  & =-\\frac{13}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
